  "summary": "Malicious code in tinkoff-pfp-block-mobile-advert-footer (npm)",
  "details": "This package is a multi-stage binary downloader. On import, it silently fingerprints the host platform and architecture, then fetches a platform-specific binary from Cloudflare Workers C2 infrastructure (oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev) at path /pkg/package. It falls back to DNS TXT-record-based payload delivery via c[.]tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site if the HTTPS fetch fails. The downloaded binary is written to /tmp/.cache_\u003crandom\u003e (Linux) or C:\\Windows\\Temp\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom\u003e.exe (Windows) and spawned as a detached background process. A state file at /tmp/.analytics_state prevents re-execution more than once per ~5.7 hours. The package exports a harmless decoy class and has no repository or documentation.",
